<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_space",
    "A space can run in a browser tab of its own, with the whole window to itself. On the character picker, choose Open in a tab. It is the same space either way — the Space tab beside the conversation keeps working for when you would rather not leave the page."
  )}
</p>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_community}>{dgettext("help_space", "Why a tab of its own")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_space",
    "The map is drawn continuously, and inside the chat it shares the browser with everything the chat is doing. In a tab of its own it does not, which is the difference you feel when several people are walking around at once."
  )}
</p>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_btn_link}>{dgettext("help_space", "The address stays good")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_space",
    "A space has no beginning and no end: it is a place, so bookmarking its address takes you back to it later. Opening it still asks the same questions as the Space tab does — a channel's space wants you in that channel, and a private space belongs to its two people. The tab always shows a way back to the chat along its bottom edge."
  )}
</p>

<p>
  {dgettext("help_space", "See also:")}
  <.help_link topic="feature-virtual-spaces">
    {dgettext("help_space", "Virtual Spaces")}
  </.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="feature-space-share">
    {dgettext("help_space", "Inviting Someone to a Space")}
  </.help_link>
</p>
